content.text:
CSS: hide mute in touch playing; landscape controls; overflow. Also mobile HUD maybe wave font. Add at end before reduced motion.

```css
body.is-touch.is-playing #muteBtn{display:none;}
@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height:560px){
 .tstick{width:96px;height:96px;bottom:max(12px,env(...))}
 .tstick.move{left:12px}.tstick.aim{right:12px}
 .tknob{width:38px;height:38px;margin:-19px}
 .tbtn.steal{width:62px;height:62px;right:120px;bottom:110px;font-size:8px}
 .tbtn.dash{width:50px;height:50px;left:124px;bottom:110px}
 #hud{...}
 #bossHud top 62px
 .banner{top:14%}
 #toast{bottom:18%}
}
```
Sticks at 96 tall + 12 bottom = top 108; arena bottom ~320; sticks on sides not center. Steal button right 120 bottom 110; aim stick right 12 width96 (covers 12..108 from right); steal at right 120 clears. Dash left 124 clears move stick (12..108). Good.

HUD on short landscape: top 10, hp/debt compact. Use same as max-width 760? It only triggers width≤760; landscape width 844 won't get compact HUD. Add `@media (max-height:560px)` compact HUD rules. Could reuse with font sizes. Add:
```css
@media (max-height:560px) and (orientation:landscape){
 #hud{padding:8px 12px 0; gap:8px}
 .hud-block{padding:5px 8px 6px; width:min(230px,28vw)}
 .hud-label{font-size:6.5px;margin-bottom:4px}
 .hp-track{height:8px}
 .sub-row{display:none}
 .debt-num span{font-size:18px}
 .debt-track{height:4px}
 .debt-warn{display:none}
 .wave-line strong{font-size:18px}
 .score{font-size:13px}
 .combo{font-size:10px}
 #hints{display:none}
 .banner{top:10%}
 .banner-title{font-size:clamp(20px,5vh,40px)}
 .banner-kicker{font-size:7px;margin-bottom:4px}
 .banner-sub{font-size:6px}
 #toast{bottom:20%;font-size:7px;padding:5px 8px}
 #bossHud{top:58px;width:52vw}
 .boss-name{font-size:6px}
}
```
The HUD side widths 28vw=236 at 844, fine. Center min-width 150; total 236+150+236+gaps 16+padding24=662, fits 844.

End panel overflow: `#end, #pause{overflow-y:auto;}` and maybe `.panel{margin:auto 0}`. In flex align center, if content taller than container it overflows top; with overflow auto and `align-items:flex-start; padding-top`? Simpler add `#end, #pause{overflow-y:auto; align-items:center;}` doesn't fix vertical centering overflow. Use `#end, #pause { align-items: flex-start; } .panel { margin: auto; }` and `min-height`? With flex container, child with margin auto centers if space, scrolls if not (auto margins become 0 when overflow). Set display flex, align-items:flex-start; justify-content:center; `.panel{margin:auto}`. Apply to both pause/end. Pause currently `justify-content:center; padding:22`. Add `align-items:flex-start` and panel margin auto. Menu unaffected. Do.

Let's apply CSS.

input.command:
cat >> styles.css <<'CSS'

/* Touch mute stays out of the thumb zone. */
body.is-touch.is-playing #muteBtn { display: none; }

