content.text:
Need mobile positioning of clock. At max-width 900, menu aligns top; clock center at 72% x, 50% y with size min(62vw=242, 86vh=726) → 242px on 390 wide, too small and on the right. The canvas menu had a large clock. Add media query:

```
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .menu-clock { left: 50%; top: 67%; width: min(116vw, 86vh); opacity:.55; }
}
```
But on 390x844: min(452,726)=452, center 50% x, 67% y=565. Top=339. Behind content; overlay gradient at top .97 hides top part, lower parts show. Fine. Yet mobile screenshot content occupies top ~450px; clock bottom ~791. Good.

On tablets 800x900: 116vw=928, 86vh=774 → 774, top 603-387=216, under content. Maybe okay.

For landscape short height 620, desktop left 72% works, width min(62vw,86vh)=533; fine. The 900 media applies if width <=900; e.g. 800x600 landscape → clock at 67% center, might overlap controls. Maybe use orientation portrait for the mobile override:

```
@media (max-width: 900px) and (orientation: portrait) { ... }
```
For landscape phones (e.g., 844x390), keep left 72%, width min(62vw=523,86vh=335)=335, okay.

Let's do portrait only.

